docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T13.log:4198:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:844:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019ScAFhwj15KgrT4jB8Uvi8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KGGVeep55c7eVz5hDjJSs8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T82.md","content":"# T82 — Phase 11 — Recovery + corrupted-event handling tests\n\n**Phase:** 11\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R79\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§Storage Design](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#storage-design), [§3. Event Log](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#3-event-log), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers two test modules that prove the daemon survives the failure modes Phase 11 names explicitly: recovery from a partial-write or crash, and handling of corrupted event payloads. Spec §Storage Design requires event-log compaction snapshots to be \"versioned and independently readable so the daemon can bootstrap from a snapshot without replaying the full history\"; spec §3 makes the event log replayable; spec §Phase 11 deliverables list \"recovery tests\" and \"corrupted-event handling\" separately. Without this suite, a single corrupted event payload could brick the daemon and a partial snapshot would silently lose history — both unacceptable per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties (\"every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable\").\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 11 deliverables: ... recovery tests; corrupted-event handling; ...\"\n\n> \"The event log should be append-only. Derived graph and memory state can be rebuilt from source files and events.\" (spec §Storage Design)\n\n> \"Event log compaction: ... at configurable intervals, write a full-state snapshot of graph and memory to a separate file, then truncate the event log to events after the snapshot timestamp. The snapshot format must be versioned and independently readable so the daemon can bootstrap from a snapshot without replaying the full history.\" (spec §Storage Design)\n\n> \"Tests for ordering, replay, corruption handling, and workspace scoping.\" (spec §Phase 2 deliverables)\n\n> \"Failure paths emit useful events without hiding errors.\" (spec §Phase 2 DoD)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R79 (contract gate) — confirms the daemon API the tests exercise is stable.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` (Phase 2 event writer/reader, payload spillover, compaction snapshot routines).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` (Phase 3 memory store).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` (SQLite connection pool, journal mode).\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (tests as documentation, error handling, observability); `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Storage Design (event log compaction snapshot, versioned format), §3 Event Log (append-only, replayable), §Phase 2 deliverables (corruption handling), §Phase 11 deliverables (recovery + corrupted-event), and §Non-Negotiable Product Properties so the recovery and corruption invariants are pinned.\n2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/recovery_tests.rs` covering:\n   - **Replay from snapshot**: produce an event log, trigger a compaction snapshot at timestamp T, append more events after T, simulate daemon restart, assert the daemon bootstraps from the snapshot + replays events-after-T to reconstruct the exact same graph + memory state.\n   - **Replay from event log only**: delete the snapshot, restart the daemon, assert it can replay the full event log to reconstruct the state (slower path, but must work).\n   - **Partial snapshot recovery**: write a snapshot file that is truncated mid-write (simulate crash during compaction); on restart, assert the daemon detects the truncated snapshot, ignores it, and falls back to full event-log replay without data loss.\n   - **Partial event write recovery**: write an event whose row is committed but whose spillover-payload row failed to commit (simulate crash between two writes); on restart, assert the daemon detects the dangling event id, emits a `recovery` event under spec §Phase 2 DoD \"failure paths emit useful events without hiding errors\", and either reconciles or quarantines the event with an explicit log line.\n   - **WAL recovery**: kill the daemon mid-write (simulate `kill -9`); on restart, assert SQLite WAL recovery completes cleanly and no events are lost.\n3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/corruption_tests.rs` covering:\n   - **Corrupted event payload**: write a valid event envelope but a corrupted (random bytes) payload to the spillover table; on read, assert the daemon emits a `corruption` event, returns an explicit error for that event, and continues processing subsequent events without crashing.\n   - **Mismatched payload hash**: write an event whose `payload_hash` does not match the actual payload bytes; on read, assert the daemon detects the hash mismatch, logs a `corruption` event, and quarantines the row.\n   - **Invalid event kind**: write a row whose `kind` column contains a string not in the 20-kind enum; on read, assert the daemon rejects the row with a clear error rather than panicking.\n   - **Invalid stable reference**: write an event with a `StableRef` pointing to a non-existent file/symbol/memory; on read, assert the daemon emits a `dangling-reference` event and surfaces the row in a quarantine query without crashing.\n   - **Truncated event log file**: physically truncate the events SQLite file mid-page; on open, assert the daemon detects the truncation, runs SQLite recovery, and continues with the events it can read while emitting a recovery log line.\n   - **Snapshot version mismatch**: write a snapshot with a higher `format_version` than the daemon supports; on read, assert the daemon refuses to bootstrap and emits a clear \"snapshot format too new\" error rather than silently loading garbage.\n4. Each test asserts the daemon survives (no panic), emits the documented recovery / corruption event under spec §Phase 2 DoD, and that the surviving state remains queryable.\n5. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` then `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::recovery_tests` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::corruption_tests` and confirm every test passes.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/recovery_tests.rs` — replay-from-snapshot, replay-from-event-log, partial-snapshot, partial-event-write, and WAL recovery scenarios.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/corruption_tests.rs` — corrupted-payload, mismatched-hash, invalid-kind, invalid-stable-ref, truncated-file, and snapshot-version-mismatch scenarios.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/recovery_tests.rs` — confirms the recovery test module exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/corruption_tests.rs` — confirms the corruption test module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::recovery_tests` — runs every recovery test and confirms every invariant assertion passes.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::corruption_tests` — runs every corruption test and confirms every invariant assertion passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split per scenario family if it exceeds).\n- Function length ≤50 lines per test; setup factored into helpers (snapshot-builder, payload-corrupter, daemon-restarter).\n- Tests as documentation: each test name describes the failure it covers (e.g. `test_partial_snapshot_falls_back_to_full_replay`, `test_corrupted_payload_quarantines_row_without_panic`).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- No silent error handling — every assertion failure panics with a message naming the scenario, the expected recovery behavior, and the observed behavior.\n- Observability: tests assert specific `tracing` events were emitted (recovery, corruption, dangling-reference) so production debuggability is validated alongside correctness.\n- Doc citation: comments cite `## Storage Design` (snapshot format), `## 3. Event Log` (replayability), `## Phase 2: Event Log Substrate` (failure paths emit useful events), `## Phase 11: Hardening` (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] Every recovery and corruption scenario named above is covered with one test per behavior.\n- [ ] Replay-from-snapshot is exercised end-to-end, supporting the runbook procedure that T86 documents.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every recovery + corruption surface from spec §Storage Design and §3 covered; partial-index (T83), migration (T84), docs (T85), runbook (T86) are sibling Phase 11 tasks, not deferrals.\n- [ ] After build, deploy per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy procedure.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101320,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":101320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"62d7b6a9-8914-4237-9396-e7e3f0ffcad0","request_id":"req_011Cb7NGicAyFMeCwEAwKwU2","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
