docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T82.log:2472:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T86.md:44:   - `## Replay from snapshot` — required by verification. The binding procedure proved viable by T82 recovery tests. Steps: (1) stop the daemon (`pkill -f lattice`); (2) verify the snapshot file exists at `.lattice/snapshots/<latest>.snap`; (3) verify the snapshot file integrity (file size, format version header, checksum); (4) move the existing `graph.db` and `memories.db` to a quarantine location for forensics; (5) start the daemon with `--bootstrap-from-snapshot <path>`; (6) confirm the daemon emits a `SnapshotBootstrap` event; (7) confirm queries return the expected pre-snapshot state plus post-snapshot replay; (8) document the post-recovery audit checklist. Cross-link to the test `test_replay_from_snapshot_reconstructs_state` in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/recovery_tests.rs`.
